WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:03.950
- [Mark] ] All right, so, Shannon.

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:05.997
Shannon, tell me about your family.

00:00:05.997 --> 00:00:09.310
Your parents were related, do you think?

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:10.573
- Yes, cousins.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.310
- [Mark] Your parents were cousins?

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:14.143
- Yeah.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:16.573
- [Mark] And that goes on here

00:00:16.573 --> 00:00:18.179
in West Virginia, doesn't it?

00:00:18.179 --> 00:00:19.720
- Unfortunately.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.280
- [Mark] And you told me your grandparents

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.380
were also related?

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.140
- [Shannon] Mm-hmm, either
my great-grandparents, or my,

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.680
I think she said my great-grandparents.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.000
But I know she said one
side of my grandparents

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.847
were cousins and, also,
and I was like, ugh.

00:00:30.847 --> 00:00:33.060
- [Mark] And you grew up where?

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.530
- Clarksburg, West Virginia,
not too far from here.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.417
- [Mark] Clarksburg,
the center of the state?

00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:40.968
Right? And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:41.958
How was it?

00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:43.483
- Abusive and dysfunctional.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.440
- [Mark] In what ways?

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.985
- Sexual abuse, physical,
emotional, and mental.

00:00:50.985 --> 00:00:52.363
- [Mark] From who?

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:58.350
- All family members, like my
dad, my brother, my cousin,

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.853
my mother, my brother, and my uncle.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:05.793
- [Mark] At what age did this start?

00:01:05.793 --> 00:01:07.203
- It started at five.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.983
- [Mark] And went on for how long?

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:14.550
- As long as I lived with my dad.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:18.653
The breaking point was
I went to, in my room,

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.960
and ended up getting my
back broke with a 2 by 4

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:25.853
from my father.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.313
That's how I met my first
husband. He was a Sergeant Cop.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:36.300
- [Mark] So, you were married?

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.163
- Yes. He's deceased though.

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:42.063
- [Mark] And how was that marriage?

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:47.570
- Abusive, but at that age, I was 19,

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:50.363
and I just wanted security.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:53.827
- [Mark] When you say abusive,

00:01:53.827 --> 00:01:55.363
what kind of stuff happened?

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:01.330
- He, my first husband cut this finger off

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:03.710
with a turkey cutter like knife,

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.870
and then broke this to the
point I had to have surgery,

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:10.073
and a pin put in it, and then it got, um,

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:15.623
infected with gangrene, and
he, then they had to take it.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.860
- [Mark] So, you lost two fingers?

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:21.693
- Yes.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:24.068
- [Mark] From?

00:02:24.068 --> 00:02:24.901
- Abuse.

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:25.850
- [Mark] And you told me one of them

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:27.920
was because he slammed
your finger in a car door?

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:28.753
On purpose?

00:02:28.753 --> 00:02:33.560
- Yeah. It is bad 'cause
he's sat there and, like,

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:37.431
when he caught the houses
on fire two months apart,

00:02:37.431 --> 00:02:41.120
then, like, he acted like the big hero

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:42.870
for comin to the hospital,

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.440
and, like, acting like he was shocked.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:46.143
But he knew he done it all along.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.780
- [Mark] Wow. And you were
married a second time?

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:55.190
- Yes. He was abusive.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:58.400
But he kicked me in my back
where I had had surgery

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.160
just right before.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.960
And I shoulda left then,

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:05.613
but I always felt like I had to have a man

00:03:05.613 --> 00:03:08.182
to make me important.

00:03:08.182 --> 00:03:10.420
- [Mark] Do you feel like
the childhood you had

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.431
kind of lead you on this path
of abusive relationships?

00:03:13.431 --> 00:03:14.404
- Very much so.

00:03:14.404 --> 00:03:15.470
- [Mark] And being
attracted to men that....

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:16.303
- Very much so.

00:03:16.303 --> 00:03:17.136
- [Mark] Are capable of that?

00:03:17.136 --> 00:03:17.969
- Uh-huh.

00:03:18.845 --> 00:03:20.920
It was so, the abuse was so bad,

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.590
that my mama said the other day

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.380
that her and granny was talking

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:29.350
and I could go turn to a woman,

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.190
or I could marry a black man,

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:34.663
'cause black men sit there
and take care of their women.

00:03:39.402 --> 00:03:41.530
- [Mark] Do you have children?

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:42.773
- I have two grown.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:49.260
When he, when Don caught the
house on fire, they were taken.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:53.970
And, then my dad,
because of being so rich,

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:58.970
sit there and paid judges
and DHHR off to get custody.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.400
So, they're in Florida now,

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:06.443
and I haven't got to see or
hear from them since 2005.

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:08.880
- [Mark] Wow.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.430
- They said that was part of the reason

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.122
I had my massive heart attack in 2015.

00:04:13.122 --> 00:04:14.002
- [Mark] You had a heart attack?

00:04:14.002 --> 00:04:14.835
- Uh-huh.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.233
- [Mark] So, your first
husband burned down the house?

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:25.810
- Yeah, the first one, Don,
he burnt the first house.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.810
He started in our daughter's
bedroom in the closet,

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.290
and then, like three days short

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.420
of it being two months apart,

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:38.340
then, it ended up having another one.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:43.340
But the, his, the officers
below him came to me,

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:46.360
each privately, three of them,

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.450
seeing if I'd leave.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.300
And I couldn't because I still believe

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:53.540
in (indistinct) salvation,
which did happen.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.300
- [Mark] Is religion a
big part of your life?

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.839
- Yes, sir.

00:04:56.839 --> 00:04:58.673
- [Mark] And which religion do you follow?

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:03.103
- Just Christianity, I
believe in the Trinity.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.403
I try doing right. I try
being good to people.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:11.860
Doing the right thing.
But I am not perfect.

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:12.693
Far from it.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:17.060
- [Mark] Do you have
any relationship today

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:19.820
with your parents and your family?

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:25.083
- My mama, uh, my grandmother
is fixin to pass away,

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:29.290
and, but I call her mom
too, 'cause she raised me

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:32.880
when all, pretty much, when
the sexual abuse, like,

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.740
whenever she could get me, she had me.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:37.773
But, she's fixin to pass, so.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:42.190
But, yeah, she wants me
and mama to be real close

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.740
when she passes.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:45.223
We've come a long way though.

00:05:46.936 --> 00:05:49.835
- [Mark] So, you have some kind
of a relationship with her?

00:05:49.835 --> 00:05:52.793
- Yeah. I told her I forgave her.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.650
Only problem is, I have
a real difficult time

00:05:56.650 --> 00:06:01.523
forgivin myself, 'cause my
dad demanded perfection.

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:09.218
- [Mark] How old are you now?

00:06:09.218 --> 00:06:12.498
- I'll be 44 November 30th of this year.

00:06:12.498 --> 00:06:15.194
- [Mark] What's the hardest
part of your life today?

00:06:15.194 --> 00:06:16.694
- Self acceptance.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:22.140
Um, not beatin myself up over,

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:27.140
like, I think from my childhood,
I expect to be perfect

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.588
'cause that's what dad demanded.

00:06:29.588 --> 00:06:34.210
And I was always scared I'd
get beat or sexually abused,

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:37.180
so I always tried to be good enough.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:42.180
And, I wanted to go back to
college and make people proud.

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:51.320
And, it's like I'm not
good enough for myself.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.670
Mama says, "You need to love yourself."

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:02.670
But when I look at myself,
I can't say that I do.

00:07:04.908 --> 00:07:08.370
I love parts of me, but
if I dare make a mistake,

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.970
I don't let myself live it down.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.133
- [Mark] And you see the relationship

00:07:15.133 --> 00:07:17.973
between your childhood and
where you are today? Right?

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:23.467
- Yeah. I'm in counselin',

00:07:23.467 --> 00:07:26.660
or, at least I was before I moved up here.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:29.750
But, so many people was
begging me to come back.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:34.623
And you can run from your problems,

00:07:35.846 --> 00:07:40.660
but until you get the quote
unquote balls to face them,

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:42.110
their always gonna haunt you.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:46.650
And, like, I used to be an addict,

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:50.660
thinking that that would be,

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:52.780
if I numb myself that it wouldn't exist.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:57.780
And, but, yeah, I tried numbing.

00:07:59.588 --> 00:08:01.653
I tried killing myself.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.350
Like, the earliest attempt,

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:07.500
well, there's only been
two actual attempts.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:11.680
And one was when I was
having right after my cousin

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:14.330
sat there and had sexually abused me,

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:16.080
and my mom had just walked in

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.143
as I was fixin to push in a knife.

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:23.590
I still have a little
indention in my chest from it.

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:25.920
- [Mark] And you were
using drugs at one point?

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.150
- Oh, yeah. Bad, bad, yeah.

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:29.780
- [Mark] It helps you forget?

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.710
- Yeah, it was, uh, like a,

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:33.860
pretty much like a numbing agent.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:38.767
And it was so bad that
I was dating a dealer,

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:41.310
and was, when I'd ask him

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:43.560
why there was so many people in and out,

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:45.560
he never would tell me.

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:48.760
But, oh yeah, major crack addict.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:51.320
And then, I told God, "If You
don't get me off this shit,

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:52.740
I'm gonna die."

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:54.973
And instantly, in that
moment, He answered.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:59.290
- [Mark] Have you used since?

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:01.290
- Um, not of crack.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:06.150
I've used meth, like, three
times, and heroin three times.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:10.850
I shot up once, well, no twice.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:14.570
They did somethin called K4.
I don't know what it was.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:15.730
- [Mark] But today you don't use?

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:16.750
- No.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:18.030
- [Mark] Do you drink?

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:21.540
- Occasionally. I try not to
make a habit of it though.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:22.400
- [Mark] It's not a problem?

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.973
- Right. It doesn't control me anymore.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:26.853
Thank God.

00:09:29.778 --> 00:09:31.200
- [Mark] So, where do you
hope your life goes from here?

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:33.700
You seem to have a good
handle on your issues.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:37.960
- I'd like to help other women, and men,

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:39.916
because a lot of people
have the misconception

00:09:39.916 --> 00:09:41.788
that men don't get abused.

00:09:41.788 --> 00:09:44.690
And yet, I have a best friend that did.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:49.690
So, I hope to be like a
abuse counselor one day.

00:09:50.139 --> 00:09:51.320
- [Mark] I think by helping others,

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.940
you can help yourself, too.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:55.963
- Right. You're only as
sick as your secrets.

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:59.173
And I was a big family secret.

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:03.070
- [Mark] All right, Shannon.

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:05.190
Thank you so much for
talking telling your story.

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:06.801
- Thank you.

00:10:06.801 --> 00:10:08.337
- [Mark] And good luck with everything.

00:10:08.337 --> 00:10:09.219
- You too.

00:10:09.219 --> 00:10:10.233
- [Mark] Thank you.

